On Sun, Oct 26, 2014 at 9:43 AM, And Rosta <and.rosta@gmail.com> wrote:

>
> If morpho-codas were unconstrained, and morpho-onsets were as per CLL
> (modulo any semivowel complications), what effects would that have on
> current lexis and usage?


I don't think it would invalidate anything, it would just open the door to
more ugly fu'ivla. The restriction on codas is based solely on aesthetics
and analogy. Lujvo never have codas heavier than a single consonant, and it
seems like a good thing to maintain that restriction for fu'ivla, which are
supposed to be as close as possible to core lojban words without
interfering with their decomposability.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

